Package: minaj
Title: Run 'gcamdata' One Chunk or One XML at a Time
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("KAIST IAM Group", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "hmcjeon@kaist.ac.kr")
Description: Runs 'gcamdata' chunks and writes single GCAM input XML files, or
    low/mid/high sets of one file, from an R session without rebuilding
    the whole data system. Every result is stored under a fingerprint of the
    chunk code, the helper functions and constant values it uses, its inputs
    and the R environment, and is reused only when that fingerprint matches.
License: ECL-2.0 | file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/GCAM-KAIST/driver_minaj
BugReports: https://github.com/GCAM-KAIST/driver_minaj/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: callr, digest, httpuv, jsonlite, pkgload, ps, stats, tibble, tools, utils, xml2
Suggests: drake, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Java (8 or later) to write XML files; bash and curl for
    the pm client
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
